received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #2047. This is the cleanup from #2033's review (round 2 should-fix).\n\nWith no active turn, the test-only `get_pending_input` drained mailbox mail. Production's `get_pending_input_for_running_task` no longer does that: it can't note the mail without a turn state. So four checks in `core/src/session/tests.rs` were exercising code production doesn't have.\n\n**Change** (tests only, plus one test-only branch removed):\n- **`session/input_queue.rs`:** the `#[cfg(test)]` `get_pending_input` delegates to `get_pending_input_for_running_task`. The `allow_untracked_mailbox` parameter and its test-only branch are removed. Production always passed `false`, so its behavior is unchanged.\n- **`session/tests.rs`:** the four checks that polled an empty slot to inspect queued mail (the reviewer's lines ~11557, ~11708, ~11766, ~13229) now use `drain_mailbox_input_items()`. That keeps each check's intent and assertion; the drain matches what the old helper did there.\n- **New test:** `get_pending_input_without_active_turn_leaves_mailbox_mail_queued` pins the helper to production. It returns nothing, and the mail stays queued.\n- **`session/stale_poll_mail_tests.rs`:** the leftover `(rev-2033)` header tag is dropped.\n\n**Results (Mac, toolchain 1.99.1):**\n- **Red** (base `input_queue.rs` + these tests): `session::` 402 passed, 1 failed, the new test only.\n- **Green:** `session::` 403 passed, 0 failed.\n- `clippy -p codex-core --tests -D warnings` and `fmt --check` both exit 0.\n- **Not run locally:** the full workspace suite. CI runs it.\n\nBase `27b317cad7a08cdb771095496e3f4b913b85afd8`, head `fb4419930e6a5e7852e92bcdf418eed1dfad16de`, DCO signed off. Raw logs are in the evidence packet linked below.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-10T09:47:03Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T09:47:0